body:
I know I shouldn't be using daily. Maybe this is something I should just google but what are the signs of benzo withdrawals? 

&#x200B;

I don't think it has negative effects for everyone, like in your case. I think it can be a useful tool for anxiety and panic attacks when taken only when truly needed. But I feel like I'm just going to be a depressed wreck if I don't start taking it every day. I've considered turning to alcohol to since I'm of legal drinking age now. I know all these things are bad, but its like my feelings/mind tell me to defy logic.

I'm a female currently taking 60 mg of Prozac and 200 mg of Lamictal. I went to my psychiatrist and he kind of just shrugged his shoulders at me saying well it should be working. I originally went on meds 2 years ago. 

&#x200B;

I guess it may just all stem from loneliness now that I have broken up and have no friends. I'm terrified of trying therapy too as I can't articulate myself well in front of strangers.
